# DustIntegration — end-to-end integration test for the ERF-Dust module.
#
# Exercises all major dust physics in a single run:
#   - Phase 6:  saltation emission (test_ustar=0 -> emission from MRF u*)
#   - Phase 7:  blast at t=2.0s, cx=1500, cy=1500, r=500m, mass=1e-4
#   - Phase 8:  suppression decay with 0.5 initial coverage
#   - Phase 9:  wind extraction from ERF-Atm (MRF u* ~ 0.56 m/s)
#   - Phase 10: emission injected into 3D atmosphere (atm_feedback=1.0)
#   - Phase 11: Stokes settling (d=7 um -> v_s ~ 4e-3 m/s)
#   - Phase 12: dry deposition (E0=3e-3, v_d ~ 5.6e-3 m/s at u*=0.56)
#   - Phase 17: PM2.5/PM10 NAAQS diagnostics
#   - Phase 18: MSHA 8h TWA at short shift (msha_shift_duration_s=5.0)
#   - Phase 21: PHREEQC deposition feedback (interval=3.0s)
#   - Phase 22: haul road emission (road active t=[1.0,-1])
#   - Phase 23: critical material flux (cm_fractions=0.001)
#
# No phase 3/4 (no PHREEQC input file, no surface maps) to keep test self-contained.
# No phase 19/20 (particles and multi-site disabled to keep runtime short).
#
# Expected results:
#   (1) Run exits code 0 at max_step=10.
#   (2) [DUST DEBUG] advance printed each step with:
#       emission_max > 0 (wind-driven + road emission).
#       cm_flux_max > 0 (cm_fractions=0.001 applied).
#       active_roads=1 from step 2 onward (road active t >= 1.0s).
#   (3) [DUST DEBUG] Phase 22: road=haul_main printed from step 2 onward.
#   (4) [DUST DEBUG] Phase 23: cm_flux_max ~ 0.001 * emission_max.
#   (5) [DUST DEBUG] Phase 18: shift ended at t=5.0s and t=10.0s
#       (msha_shift_duration_s=5.0).
#   (6) dust_diag.dat: 10 rows; emission_total > 0 each step.
#   (7) dust_naaqs.csv: 10 rows; PM10_max > 0.
#   (8) msha_exposure.csv: 10 rows; TWA_max increasing.
#   (9) dust_dep_feedback.dat: written at t=3.0, 6.0, 9.0s and final step.
#  (10) dust_road_diag.csv: rows for haul_main from step 2 onward.
#  (11) dust_cm_budget.csv: 10 data groups (1 domain + 1 unassigned per step).
#  (12) [DUST COUPLING] F_dust_max > 0 from step 2 onward (explicit lag).
#  (13) Blast event at step 4 (t=2.0s): emission_max spikes higher than adjacent steps.
#  (14) All output files created with valid CSV headers.
#
# Note: Phase 15 (AMR blending) is not tested here (amr.max_level=0).
# Note: Phases 3,4 surface maps and PHREEQC files are disabled (empty paths).
#
# References:
#   Marticorena & Bergametti (1995). https://doi.org/10.1029/95JD00690
#   Shao & Lu (2000). https://doi.org/10.1029/2000JD900304
#   Zhang et al. (2001). https://doi.org/10.1016/S1352-2310(00)00326-5
#   Hong & Pan (1996). https://doi.org/10.1175/1520-0493(1996)124<2322:NBLVDI>2.0.CO;2

